---
import Container from "@/components/common/Container/Container.astro";
import { OWNER_EMAIL } from "@/siteConstants";
import styles from "./Privacy.module.css";

const LAST_UPDATED = "November 15, 2026";
const TURNSTILE_PRIVACY_URL =
  "https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/";
const BC_PRIVACY_COMMISSIONER_URL = "https://www.oipc.bc.ca/";
---

<main>
  <div class={styles.intro} data-ground="forest" data-hero>
    <Container>
      <div class={styles.column}>
        <p class={styles.updated}>Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>
        <h1 class={styles.heading}>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class={styles.summary}>
          This is my personal site. I'm Takafumi Megumi, and I wrote this page
          myself. The site has no ads and no third-party trackers. I only
          receive what you send me through the forms, plus anonymous records of
          page views.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </div>

  <Container>
    <div class:list={[styles.column, styles.body]}>
      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        I am. For any question about your information, email me at {OWNER_EMAIL}
        .
      </p>

      <h2>What I collect and why</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>When you book a call.</strong> Your name, your email address,
        and, if you add it, what you'd like to talk about. I use them to set up
        the call and to get in touch about it. Booking creates an event on my
        Google Calendar, Google emails an invitation to the address you entered,
        and the site emails me the details.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>When you send a message.</strong> Your name, your email address,
        and your message. I use them to reply. The message reaches me by email.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>When you submit either form.</strong> Cloudflare Turnstile
        checks that a person is sending the form. It looks at signals such as
        your IP address and browser details, and it may use cookies and browser
        storage that Cloudflare describes as strictly necessary for detecting
        bots. It runs only when you submit a form.{" "}
        <a href={TURNSTILE_PRIVACY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Cloudflare's Turnstile Privacy Addendum
        </a>{" "}
        has the details. The site also uses your IP address for a moment to stop
        a burst of submissions, and does not keep it.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>When you view a page.</strong> The site records that a page was
        opened, how long it stayed on screen, how far it was scrolled, whether a
        call was booked, a message was sent, or a case study was read, and a tag
        from the link you followed, if it had one. I use this to see which pages
        are read. It uses no cookies. It does not record your IP address or the
        page you came from, and it stores nothing in your browser to recognize
        you later.
      </p>

      <h2>Your consent, and how to withdraw it</h2>
      <p>
        When you submit a form, you agree to the uses above. You can ask me to
        delete what you sent at any time.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can turn off page-view measurement in this browser:{" "}
        <a href="/privacy/?measure=off">Turn measurement off</a>. To remember
        that choice, the site saves one small marker in your browser.{" "}
        <a href="/privacy/?measure=on">Turn it back on</a> removes the marker.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else handles your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the site, runs the bot check,
          delivers messages to my inbox, and stores the page-view records.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google</strong> holds the calendar events and invitations, and
          the emails I receive.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sentry</strong> receives error reports from the server. They
          contain no information about you.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I don't sell your information or share it for any other purpose. These
        companies process information on servers outside Canada, mainly in the
        United States, where authorities may be able to access it under local
        law.
      </p>

      <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The site itself stores nothing you enter in the forms.</li>
        <li>
          Messages and bookings stay in my inbox and calendar while they are
          useful for our conversation. I delete them when you ask.
        </li>
        <li>
          Page-view records are deleted automatically after about three months.
        </li>
        <li>
          Cloudflare keeps short-lived logs of requests to the site, which
          include technical details such as IP addresses.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How I protect it</h2>
      <p>
        The site keeps no copy of what you send, so there is nothing on it to
        leak. Connections to the site are encrypted. Only I can access my inbox
        and calendar, and the account is protected with two-step verification.
      </p>

      <h2>Seeing or correcting your information</h2>
      <p>
        Email me to see, correct, or delete the information I have about you. I
        will reply within 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If you have a concern about how I've handled your information, email me
        first. If we can't resolve it, you can contact the{" "}
        <a href={BC_PRIVACY_COMMISSIONER_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Office of the Information and Privacy Commissioner for British
          Columbia
        </a>
        .
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, I will update this page and the date at the top.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Container>
</main>
